    "stac_version": "1.1.0",
    "description": "This dataset contains salt marsh nutrient data to determine the biogeochemical impact of elevated nutrient loading on ecosystem carbon dynamics and nitrate reduction pathways (denitrification and dissimilatory nitrate reduction to ammonium (DNRA)) in plots dominated by either Juncus roemerianus or Spartina alterniflora that were collocated in a northern Gulf of Mexico salt marsh. The nutrients measured in this dataset include saltmarsh denitrification potential, anaerobic ammonium oxidation (anammox) potential, porewater nutrient concentrations, gross primary productivity, ecosystem respiration, and others. This data is available in .csv format.",
